            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0208" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/6073</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.45 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3053. [From Endicott to] American Red Cross:</p>
                <p>1872. Have seen general commanding Archangel area who is now in London. He
                    instructs us not to send foodstuffs to Archangel as it is not necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
